    <string name="feature_settings_about_text">A local music player. Free, no ads, no account. Made in Belém, Brazil, with AI assistance under the author’s direction and review.</string>
    <string name="feature_settings_privacy_text">Your library, your settings and your listening stats stay on your device only. The app has no account, no ads and sends nothing about you anywhere.\n\nWhen you open an artist, the app asks Deezer for public information about them (photo, popular songs, discography) using only the artist’s name. For the biography, it asks Last.fm (through our own server, which only adds the access key) using the artist’s name. Scrobbling to Last.fm, when it arrives, only happens if you turn it on.\n\nLyrics are looked up on LRCLIB only when you open them, using the song title, artist, album and length. When you share a song, the app looks it up on Deezer and asks song.link for the matching YouTube Music link. Fixing tags automatically asks Deezer and Last.fm using the song’s title, artist and length, only when you tap Search. “Check for updates” only contacts GitHub when you tap it.\n\nFriends is optional. If you create a profile, our server keeps your name and @, and delivers your messages and song recommendations, deleting each one as soon as it reaches the other phone; your conversations stay only on your phone. What you’re listening to is shared only if you turn it on, and only with people you talk to. Audio files are never sent.\n\nThe only permission requested is music and audio, to read the songs on your phone. When you save tags, Android asks you to allow changing that file. The app doesn’t ask for photos, videos, contacts or location.</string>
